{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing stitch task #5410 for the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement srd060-date requirements R3.1-R3.4 (UTC mode and reference time) in `cmd/date/main.go` and add corresponding differential tests in `cmd/date/date_test.go`. The requirements are:\n   - R3.1: `-u`/`--utc`/`--universal` must display date in UTC\n   - R3.2: `-r FILE`/`--reference=FILE` must display last modification time of FILE\n   - R3.3: When referenced file doesn't exist, print error to stderr and exit 1\n   - R3.4: Must not read from stdin; write formatted output to stdout only\n   \n   The acceptance criteria require: `go vet` passes, `go build` succeeds, R3.1-R3.4 are fully implemented, and differential tests pass against `gdate`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` comparing Go binary against GNU `gdate`\n   - `testutils.DiffTest` struct with fields: Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - strftime-style format string parsing in Go\n   - Epoch-based deterministic date testing with `@EPOCH` syntax\n   - `LC_ALL=C` environment for deterministic locale behavior\n   - Binary name normalization for stderr comparison between Go and reference binaries\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd060-date.yaml`\n     - Source of truth for R3.1-R3.4 requirements\n     - R3.1: UTC mode via `-u`/`--utc`/`--universal`\n     - R3.2: Reference file mtime via `-r FILE`/`--reference=FILE`\n     - R3.3: Error handling for missing reference file\n     - R3.4: No stdin reading, stdout-only output\n     - Non-goals: no `-s/--set`, no `--rfc-3339`/`-