e containing: role definition, repository file list, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements R3.1-R3.4, design decisions, acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Update `cmd/date/main.go` header comment to include R3.4\n   - Add differential tests in `cmd/date/date_test.go` for:\n     - R3.1: UTC mode tests (`-u`, `--utc`, `--universal` with format strings)\n     - R3.2: Reference file tests (`-r FILE`, `--reference=FILE`)\n     - R3.3: Missing reference file error test (exit code 1)\n     - R3.4: Verify stdout-only output (implicitly covered by all tests)\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/date/...`\n   - Run `go build -o bin/date ./cmd/date/`\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/date/... -count=1`\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, date_test.go) and was about to begin implementing. I had analyzed that R3.1-R3.3 are already implemented in main.go, and the primary work is:\n   1. Update the header comment in main.go from `R3.1-R3.3` to `R3.1-R3.4`\n   2. Add a new `TestDiffUTCAndReference` (or similar) test function in date_test.go with DiffTest entries covering UTC mode, reference file, missing file error\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Modify `cmd/date/main.go` to update the header comment to include R3.4, then modify `cmd/date/date_test.go` to add differential tests for R3.1-R3.4. The tests should include:\n   - UTC mode with `-u` flag combined with epoch dates and format strings\n   - `--utc` and `--universal` long flag variants\n   - `-r /dev/null` reference file with format string\n   - `--reference=/dev/null` long flag variant\n   - `-r nonexistent_file` with ExitCode: 1 and normalizeBinaryName\n   Then run `go vet`, `go build`, and `go test` to verify acceptance criteria.\n\n   Direct quote from task: \"Implement srd060-date requirement R3.1 as